  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nSunday and Monday will be drier with warmer afternoons and more \npartly to mostly cloudy skies. Highs should climb into the upper 70s \nto middle 80s both days with warmer temperatures south of Highway \n90/I-10. Weak shortwave ridging will be the reason for warmer and \ndrier weather both Sunday and Monday before a powerful trough digs \nover the southern Rockies Monday. This will send a stronger cold \nfront in our direction on Election Day, with the potential for \nthunderstorms, some strong to severe with large hail and damaging \nwinds possible. This would be more of a line of storms rather than \nthe large, stratiform type rain we've had the last 24-36 hours. \nBeyond Tuesday, the pattern turns drier and cooler. Each morning \nwill start in the 40s and 50s followed by afternoons in the 70s.",
